### Units & Chapter Titles in Class X Mathematics

**Unit I: Number Systems**

- Real Numbers (covering the Fundamental Theorem of Arithmetic, proofs of irrationality for √2, √3, √5, etc.)&#x20;

**Unit II: Algebra**

- Polynomials (zeros and the relationship between zeros and coefficients of a quadratic polynomial)
- Pair of Linear Equations in Two Variables (graphical and algebraic methods including consistency/inconsistency)
- Quadratic Equations (standard form, real roots, discriminant, and real-life applications)
- Arithmetic Progressions (nth term, sum of n terms, and applications)&#x20;

**Unit III: Coordinate Geometry**

- Distance Formula and Section (Internal Division) Formula&#x20;

**Unit IV: Geometry**

- Triangles (similarity—Basic Proportionality Theorem, criteria for similarity)
- Circles (tangent properties: perpendicular to radius, equal tangents from an external point)&#x20;

**Unit V: Trigonometry**

- Introduction to Trigonometry (trigonometric ratios of standard angles, their existence, relationships)
- Trigonometric Identities (e.g., sin²A + cos²A = 1)
- Heights and Distances (problems involving angles of elevation and depression of 30°, 45°, 60°)&#x20;

**Unit VI: Mensuration**

- Areas Related to Circles (sectors and segments with central angles 60°, 90°, 120°)
- Surface Areas and Volumes (combinations of cubes, cuboids, spheres, hemispheres, cylinders, cones)&#x20;

**Unit VII: Statistics & Probability**

- Statistics (mean, median, and mode of grouped data)
- Probability (classical definition and simple probability problems)&#x20;

